# Turning a manifested creature face up is a special action the rules give (CR 116.2b, 701.40b), not an ability of the
# face-down permanent, so "creatures lose all abilities" doesn't stop it (Whisperwood Elemental's ruling: a manifested
# creature card can be turned face up after losing its abilities). The opening is the other manifest scenarios': on Bot2's
# upkeep Abhorrent Oculus manifests dread and Snapcaster Mage goes onto the battlefield face down. On Bot1's turn 3 Dress
# Down makes every creature lose all abilities, and Bot1 still turns the Mage face up for {1}{U}.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Wheel of Fortune
Island x4
Mox Sapphire
Sol Ring
Abhorrent Oculus
Dress Down
Mox Pearl
Island x2
Snapcaster Mage
Lightning Bolt
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x7
Forest
Haywire Mite
Swamp x11

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Wheel of Fortune.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Abhorrent Oculus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Choose(Island; Island; Island; Island; Black Lotus; Wheel of Fortune)
[T2 Bot2.Upkeep]
Bot1.Arrange(Snapcaster Mage | Lightning Bolt)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Haywire Mite.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dress Down.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield..FaceDown = true
Bot1.Battlefield.#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Choose(Assign mana)
? Bot1.Battlefield = Abhorrent Oculus; Dress Down; Island; Mountain; Mox Pearl; Mox Sapphire; Snapcaster Mage; Sol Ring
? Bot1.Battlefield.Snapcaster Mage.FaceDown = (absent)
[T3 Bot1.End]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Snapcaster Mage.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Snapcaster Mage.Toughness = 1
